| !Run for Vanilla Conquer: Red Alert
Set VanillaRA$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <VanillaRA$Dir>.!Sprites
| Low resolution: 1 runs the game at 320x200 (the DOS version's size), about twice
| as fast, for slower machines; 0 runs it at 640x400. It uses the game's own 320x200
| graphics, with less of the map on screen and a smaller sidebar.
Set VanillaRA$LowRes 0
| Movie sound: 1 plays movies with their sound, 0 without. Unset, movies are silent
| before RISC OS 5, as the intro crashed with sound on a real Risc PC (see !Help).
| Set VanillaRA$MovieSound 1
| SharedUnixLibrary is normally in !System; fall back to the copy shipped here.
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 RMLoad <VanillaRA$Dir>.Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error Vanilla Conquer needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later
| DigitalRenderer plays the sound (via SDL). Without it the game runs silently.
RMEnsure DigitalRenderer 0.56 IfThere System:Modules.DRenderer Then RMLoad System:Modules.DRenderer
RMEnsure DigitalRenderer 0.56 RMLoad <VanillaRA$Dir>.Modules.DRenderer
| The heap is in a dynamic area of its own (see redalert/startup.cpp).
WimpSlot -min 6000K -max 6000K
Run <VanillaRA$Dir>.!RunImage %*0 >/<VanillaRA$Dir>/stdout 2>/<VanillaRA$Dir>/stderr
